1
00:00:00,123 --> 00:00:00,995
You're running a race

2
00:00:00,995 --> 00:00:02,442
and something stabs you

3
00:00:02,442 --> 00:00:04,367
under the RIBS!

4
00:00:04,410 --> 00:00:05,420
Relax.

5
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:06,780
It's not a cramp.

6
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:07,733
Best guess?

7
00:00:07,770 --> 00:00:09,500
Your insides are chafing.

8
00:00:09,542 --> 00:00:10,363
Your belly has

9
00:00:10,363 --> 00:00:11,915
a slippery lining:

10
00:00:11,915 --> 00:00:13,481
one layer on the wall,

11
00:00:13,481 --> 00:00:15,033
one around your organs.

12
00:00:15,081 --> 00:00:16,612
Run, and your organs

13
00:00:16,612 --> 00:00:17,533
bounce.

14
00:00:17,570 --> 00:00:18,756
Add a full stomach...

15
00:00:18,756 --> 00:00:19,647
and the layers

16
00:00:19,647 --> 00:00:20,433
rub.

17
00:00:20,475 --> 00:00:21,182
The outer layer

18
00:00:21,182 --> 00:00:23,300
feels sharp pain.

19
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:24,500
That's why it jabs

20
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:25,734
ONE spot...

21
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:26,780
and stops

22
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:27,900
when you stop.

23
00:00:28,004 --> 00:00:29,349
Subscribe...

24
00:00:29,349 --> 00:00:31,167
a camel is involved.

25
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:32,541
It's not from breathing hard,

26
00:00:32,541 --> 00:00:33,033
either.

27
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:33,853
People get stitches

28
00:00:33,853 --> 00:00:35,047
riding horses...

29
00:00:35,047 --> 00:00:36,410
and camels.

30
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:37,826
Sitting down.

31
00:00:37,944 --> 00:00:38,344
Shakespeare

32
00:00:38,239 --> 00:00:39,890
wrote about this pain...

33
00:00:39,890 --> 00:00:40,750
and science

34
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:42,940
STILL isn't sure.

35
00:00:43,030 --> 00:00:44,450
So slow down,

36
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:45,767
lean forward...

37
00:00:45,767 --> 00:00:46,981
and never trust

38
00:00:46,981 --> 00:00:48,190
a camel.

